  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This coastal trail links Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer to Bandol via a "sentier des Douaniers"-type path that follows the coast through Mediterranean garrigue scrubland, passing the Port d'Alon cove — a lovely stop protected by the Conservatoire du Littoral. Depending on the stretch chosen, allow between 6-7 km (Bandol ↔ Port d'Alon) and up to 12 km for the full route to the Port de la Madrague in Saint-Cyr.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Keep your dog on a leash on the coastal trail, notably because of sections overlooking the cliff. According to the Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer tourist office, the pebble beach of the Port d'Alon cove and the area behind it are banned to dogs from 9am to 5pm from 1 April to 30 September; outside this period, dogs are allowed there, on a leash. A section of the trail between Pointe Grenier and Pointe Fauconnière has been closed by municipal order (reported by Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme): ask the Bandol tourist office before setting out. The ground is rocky, typical of garrigue scrubland, with little shade over most of the route: bring plenty of water for your dog. The Port d'Alon car park is paid every day from 8am to 5pm from 1 April to 30 September (upper car park: €5 for the day); car parks also exist in Bandol (Casino, Central, Stade) and on the Saint-Cyr side at Port de la Madrague.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: come in spring or autumn instead — free parking at Port d'Alon, less heat for your dog on this lightly shaded trail, and no time restriction on the beach.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer and Bandol, at the two ends of the trail, each offer ways to extend the outing: the <a href="/en/fiche-dogwash-saint-cyr-sur-mer">dog wash in Saint-Cyr-sur-Mer</a> to rinse off your companion after the walk, and on the Bandol side, <a href="/en/fiche-bandol">Bandol Dog Beach</a> or <a href="/en/fiche-hebergement-bandol">dog-friendly accommodation</a> if you're extending your stay in the area.</p>
